{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH, slow to anger.</b> For the righteous and for the wicked. When Moses ascended on high, he found the Holy One, blessed be He, sitting and writing 'YHWH, slow to anger.' He said to Him: for the righteous? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: also for the wicked. He said to Him: let the wicked perish! He said to him: by your life, you will need this thing. When Israel sinned with the calf and with the spies, Moses prayed before Him with 'slow to anger.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: did you not say to Me, for the righteous? He said to Him: and did you not say to me, also for the wicked? <b>Let the power of my Lord grow</b> — to fulfill Your word (Sanhedrin 111)." "<b>And pardons.</b> For those who repent." "<b>He will by no means clear.</b> For those who do not repent (Yoma 86a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :register {:flags {0 ["Lord"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:50.459853376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}